IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `oapa-nouns`
IMPORT `oapa-danger-neglect-explosives`

-- Offences against the Person Act 1861 -- TESTS for oapa-danger-neglect-explosives.l4
-- (sections 26 to 31).  Every expected value was decided from the section's text before
-- the assertion was written, and is stated beside it.  OF is positional; each group has
-- a ruler naming the columns in DECLARE order.

§ `Tests: sections 26 to 31`

§§ `Section 26`

-- legally liable, wilfully refused or neglected, had a lawful excuse, unlawfully,
-- maliciously, did or caused bodily harm, life endangered, health permanently injured
`s26 refused, life endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 refused, health permanently injured` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s26 refused, no result` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s26 refused with a lawful excuse` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 not legally liable` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 neglect was not wilful` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 harm, life endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 harm, health injured` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s26 harm, not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 harm, not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s26 harm, no result` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s26 no liability, harm, result` MEANS `Conduct under section 26` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 refused, life endangered`
#ASSERT `s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 refused, health permanently injured`
-- The reading taken (see NOTES.md, fork 26a): the result clause governs the refusal
-- limb too, so a refusal that endangers no life and injures no health is not caught.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 refused, no result`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 refused with a lawful excuse`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 not legally liable`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 neglect was not wilful`)
#ASSERT `s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 harm, life endangered`
#ASSERT `s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 harm, health injured`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 harm, not malicious`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 harm, not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 harm, no result`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 26: neglecting or harming an apprentice or servant` `s26 no liability, harm, result`)
#ASSERT `s 26: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 26: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 27`

-- unlawfully, abandoned or exposed a child, the child's age in complete months, life
-- endangered, health permanently injured
`s27 aged 23 months, life endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, TRUE, 23, TRUE, FALSE
`s27 aged 24 months, life endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, TRUE, 24, TRUE, FALSE
`s27 newborn, life endangered` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, TRUE, 0, TRUE, FALSE
`s27 aged 12 months, health injured` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, TRUE, 12, FALSE, TRUE
`s27 aged 12 months, no result` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, TRUE, 12, FALSE, FALSE
`s27 aged 12 months, not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF FALSE, TRUE, 12, TRUE, FALSE
`s27 aged 12 months, not abandoned or exposed` MEANS `Conduct under section 27` OF TRUE, FALSE, 12, TRUE, FALSE

-- "under the age of two years": 23 complete months is under, 24 is not.
#ASSERT `s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 23 months, life endangered`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 24 months, life endangered`)
#ASSERT `s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 newborn, life endangered`
#ASSERT `s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 12 months, health injured`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 12 months, no result`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 12 months, not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 27: abandoning or exposing a child under two years` `s27 aged 12 months, not abandoned or exposed`)
#ASSERT `s 27: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 27: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 28`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, by the explosion, burnt, maimed, disfigured, disabled,
-- grievous bodily harm
`s28 burnt` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 maimed` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 disfigured` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 disabled` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s28 grievous bodily harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s28 explosion, no harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 harm, not by explosion` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s28 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 28` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 burnt`
#ASSERT `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 maimed`
#ASSERT `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 disfigured`
#ASSERT `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 disabled`
#ASSERT `s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 grievous bodily harm`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 explosion, no harm`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 harm, not by explosion`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 28: causing bodily injury by an explosion` `s28 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 28: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
-- two options: penal servitude for life, or imprisonment (term not stated)
#ASSERT `s 28: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 29`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, caused an explosion, sent or delivered a dangerous thing, put
-- or laid a corrosive fluid or destructive substance, cast or applied one to a person,
-- intent to burn/maim/disfigure/disable, intent to do grievous bodily harm, injury effected
`s29 explosion, intent to burn` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s29 sent a dangerous thing, intent to burn` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s29 put or laid at a place, intent to burn` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s29 threw corrosive fluid at a person, intent to do GBH` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s29 threw corrosive fluid, intent to do GBH, injury effected` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE
`s29 explosion, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s29 intent, no act` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s29 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s29 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 29` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 explosion, intent to burn`
#ASSERT `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 sent a dangerous thing, intent to burn`
#ASSERT `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 put or laid at a place, intent to burn`
#ASSERT `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 threw corrosive fluid at a person, intent to do GBH`
-- "whether any bodily injury be effected or not": injury changes nothing
#ASSERT `s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 threw corrosive fluid, intent to do GBH, injury effected`
-- injury effected without the intent is not the offence of this section
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 explosion, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 intent, no act`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 29: causing an explosion, or sending or applying a dangerous thing, with intent` `s29 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 29: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
#ASSERT `s 29: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for life`, `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 30`

-- unlawfully, maliciously, placed or threw an explosive in/into/upon/against/near a
-- building, ship or vessel, intent to do bodily injury, an explosion took place, injury effected
`s30 placed, intent, nothing happened` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s30 placed, intent, explosion and injury` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`s30 placed, no intent` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s30 intent, did not place` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s30 not unlawful` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s30 not malicious` MEANS `Conduct under section 30` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE

-- "whether or not any explosion take place, and whether or not any bodily injury be effected"
#ASSERT `s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 placed, intent, nothing happened`
#ASSERT `s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 placed, intent, explosion and injury`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 placed, no intent`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 intent, did not place`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 not unlawful`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 30: placing an explosive near a building, ship or vessel, with intent` `s30 not malicious`)
#ASSERT `s 30: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS felony
-- fourteen years = 168 months; the second option's term is not stated
#ASSERT `s 30: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` (`for a term not exceeding` 168), `imprisonment` `for a term the text does not state`

§§ `Section 31`

-- the engine is calculated to destroy life or inflict GBH, set or placed it, intended it to
-- destroy or inflict harm, intended it to be set so that it may, knowingly and wilfully
-- permitted it to continue, a vermin gin or trap, set from sunset to sunrise in a dwelling house
`s31 set, intent to harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s31 set so that it may harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s31 set, no intent of either kind` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`s31 permitted to continue, no intent of its own` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s31 permitted an engine not calculated to harm` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE
`s31 set with intent, a vermin gin or trap` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE
`s31 set with intent, in a dwelling house from sunset to sunrise` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`s31 permitted, in a dwelling house from sunset to sunrise` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE
`s31 permitted, a vermin gin or trap` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE
`s31 set with intent, in a dwelling house but not from sunset to sunrise` MEANS `Conduct under section 31` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set, intent to harm`
#ASSERT `s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set so that it may harm`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set, no intent of either kind`)
-- the deeming limb: permitting it to continue is treated as setting it with the intent
#ASSERT `s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 permitted to continue, no intent of its own`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 permitted an engine not calculated to harm`)
-- the two provisos
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set with intent, a vermin gin or trap`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set with intent, in a dwelling house from sunset to sunrise`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 permitted, in a dwelling house from sunset to sunrise`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 permitted, a vermin gin or trap`)
-- the dwelling-house proviso covers sunset to sunrise only: by day it does not apply
#ASSERT `s 31: setting a spring gun or man trap` `s31 set with intent, in a dwelling house but not from sunset to sunrise`
#ASSERT `s 31: what the text calls the offence` EQUALS misdemeanor
#ASSERT `s 31: the sentences the text states` EQUALS LIST `penal servitude` `for a term the text does not state`
